{{ bos_token }}{% raw %}<start_of_turn>user
Find the domain of the expression $\frac{\sqrt{x-2}}{\sqrt{5-x}}$.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
The expressions inside each square root must be non-negative. So $x-2\ge 0$, giving $x\ge 2$, and $5-x\ge 0$, giving $x\le 5$. The denominator cannot be zero, so $5-x>0$, i.e. $x<5$. Therefore the domain is $[2,5)$. The final answer is $\boxed{[2,5)}$.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>user
There are 15 trees in the grove. Grove workers will plant trees in the grove today. After they are done, there will be 21 trees. How many trees did the grove workers plant today?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
There were 15 trees originally and 21 after planting, so the workers planted $21 - 15 = 6$ trees. The final answer is $\boxed{6}$.<end_of_turn>
